        <div><a name="_portuguese" id="_portuguese"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.35 Portuguese</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_c38c6349-e180-43ed-9b17-c29681acda56" id="_c38c6349-e180-43ed-9b17-c29681acda56"></a>given name(s) + mother&#x2019;s patronymic name(s) + father&#x2019;s patronymic name(s)</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_8d7b8008-a0c7-4942-a468-dc21838a0a61" id="_8d7b8008-a0c7-4942-a468-dc21838a0a61"></a>Portuguese often have two personal names, although the first may at times be used on its own.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_f5cd2a75-cedc-4445-9681-9ed890711ed2" id="_f5cd2a75-cedc-4445-9681-9ed890711ed2"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>George Agostinho Baptista da Silva.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_e4e700f4-18ce-4ec1-b8b9-bc42910920e9" id="_e4e700f4-18ce-4ec1-b8b9-bc42910920e9"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Ant&#xF3;nio Caetano de Abreu Freire Egas Moniz, Nobel prize winner. He was the child of Fernando de Pina Rezende Abreu and Maria do Rosario de Almeida e Sousa.</p></div></div>
