        <div><a name="_slavic" id="_slavic"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.40 Slavic</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_228a62a5-b301-4a2f-a02c-a2ee81bad6e2" id="_228a62a5-b301-4a2f-a02c-a2ee81bad6e2"></a>name components:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo36;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    family name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo36;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    given name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo36;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    patronymic name
  </p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_26da1fb0-0a57-4b52-88ed-13e017fdbcbf" id="_26da1fb0-0a57-4b52-88ed-13e017fdbcbf"></a>Slavic naming applies to Russian, Ukrainian, Belorussian,
Bulgaria, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Serbia and Macedonia,
as well as some populations of Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan, Uzbekistan and Turkmenistan.</p>
<div><a name="_typical_name_patterns_12" id="_typical_name_patterns_12"></a><p class="h3Annex">B.40.1 Typical name patterns</p>

  <p class="TableTitle" align="center">Table B.46</p><div align="center"><table style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;" class="MsoISOTable" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><a name="_ef2169e4-7e13-4a02-a023-064afae8450b" id="_ef2169e4-7e13-4a02-a023-064afae8450b"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">patronymic name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</div>
<div><a name="_examples_12" id="_examples_12"></a><p class="h3Annex">B.40.2 Examples</p><div class="example"><a name="_13f2a1d4-5ad7-4671-967f-c25f3434b41f" id="_13f2a1d4-5ad7-4671-967f-c25f3434b41f"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x418;&#x432;&#x430;&#x301;&#x43D; &#x41A;&#x43E;&#x43D;&#x441;&#x442;&#x430;&#x43D;&#x442;&#x438;&#x301;&#x43D;&#x43E;&#x432;&#x438;&#x447; &#x410;&#x439;&#x432;&#x430;&#x437;&#x43E;&#x301;&#x432;&#x441;&#x43A;&#x438;&#x439; (&#x201C;Ivan Konstantinovich Aivazovsky&#x201D;). Ivan is the given name, Konstantinovich the patronymic name, Aivazovsky the family name.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_1f7e5fdd-810f-4b05-97e7-ec2322c4ab89" id="_1f7e5fdd-810f-4b05-97e7-ec2322c4ab89"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x41E;&#x43B;&#x435;&#x43A;&#x441;&#x430;&#x43D;&#x434;&#x440; &#x406;&#x432;&#x430;&#x43D;&#x43E;&#x432;&#x438;&#x447; &#x411;&#x456;&#x43B;&#x430;&#x448;, (&#x201C;Oleksandr Ivanovych Bilash&#x201D;).  Oleksandr is the given name, Ivanovych the patronymic name, Bilash the family name.</p></div></div></div>
